<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Yorktown</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1781">1781</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Yorktown, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, was the last major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>. From late September to 19 October 1781 a combined American and French army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> and the Comte de Rochambeau, with a French fleet blocking relief by sea, besieged the British army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis">Lord Cornwallis</a>, whose surrender led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to open peace negotiations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-yorktown.jpg" alt="Siege of Yorktown" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Trumbull · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surrender_of_Lord_Cornwallis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
